    "snippet": "With enough moisture this short wave may provide enough extra lift to produce light isolated showers over the White Mountains, and can already be seen on satellite beginning to form. The increasing moisture combined with an upper- level jet streak moving through the Great Basin, increasing the upper-level forcing for ascent, will cause areas of scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms to break out, mainly over central and southern AZ Saturday afternoon/evening.",
